# Icon-first UX (strict)

Unless Govinda explicitly asks for text labels:

- Navigation controls are **icons only** (Home, Back, Close) — no text buttons like “Home” / “Back”.
- Sticky top bar: icon Home + icon Back + **breadcrumbs** for place.
- Breadcrumb segments that are links use **link color** plus a small **link icon** after the label.
- In-content links: link color + link icon after the context — not plain green text buttons.
- Toolbars / place editors / chrome actions: **icons only** (drag tools, layer, rotate, lock, download, reset, etc.).

## Tooltips (required on every icon)

- Every icon control **must** expose a short human tooltip: `aria-label` + `title` + `data-tip` (same string).
- Tooltips name the action, not the glyph (“Bring forward”, “Lock for production”, “Prompts · G inbound”).
- Use the shared chrome tip style (`.ico-tip` / `[data-tip]`) so hover/focus shows a readable tip — do not ship bare icons with no tip.
- When lock/state toggles an icon, update `aria-label`, `title`, and `data-tip` together.

## Rules / prompts icons

- Show a prompt/rules icon **only** where a prompt JSON or phase note actually exists.
- Keep it **subtle** (low contrast) — agent affordance, not primary UI.
- Do not scatter rules icons on every card for decoration.
- Still give each rules icon a tooltip (e.g. “Prompts · Phase 2”).

## Image pickers

- Prefer lightbox/pop-up on thumbnail click over an extra inner page when the candidates are already visible.
